    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## n8n AI Agent × Check Point MCP gateway\nn8n's own AI Agent uses **every Check Point tool** the EKS gateway exposes, over MCP (streamable HTTP).\n\n**Setup (once)**\n1. Create an **MCP OAuth2** credential: Dynamic Client Registration **off**, grant type **Client Credentials**, Access Token URL = `CHKP_TOKEN_URL`, Client ID + Secret from `chkpmcpeks endpoints --reveal-secret`, scope `chkp-mcp/invoke`.\n2. Select it in **Refresh gateway token** and **Check Point MCP gateway** (set both URLs to `CHKP_MCP_URL`).\n3. **Claude** (Anthropic credential) is the main model; **OpenAI** is the fallback. Swap either for any tool-calling model.\n4. Chat: *What is the reputation of https://www.checkpoint.com?*\n\n**Why the token step:** the MCP node (n8n 2.28) sends the token stored on the credential but does not fetch a client-credentials token itself. The HTTP Request node does, saves it on the same credential, and renews it on a 401.\n\nThe gateway hides mutating tools (read-only policy) and never forwards credential headers.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "7a4d2e3f-0006-4b00-9000-000000000006",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -280
      ]
    }
